5
2 2
0 0
DONE

      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #29, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ ⎕ES's LRM-recommended idiom (Figure 40, p.353) for giving a
      ⍝ defined function a VALENCE ERROR when called with the wrong
      ⍝ number of arguments -- ⎕ES(2≠⎕NC 'Y')/5 1 -- used to fail when Y
      ⍝ (the declared but, in a monadic call, unsupplied left argument)
      ⍝ was still reachable from UserFunction::set_locked_error_info():
      ⍝ it unconditionally called Symbol::get_apl_value() on Y, which
      ⍝ throws VALUE ERROR for an unbound symbol, silently replacing the
      ⍝ intended ⎕ES-simulated error.
      ⍝
      )ERASE ROUND2
∇Z←Y ROUND2 X
 ⎕ES(2≠⎕NC 'Y')/5 1  ⍝SIGNAL VALENCE ERROR
 Z←(10*-Y)×⌊.5+X×10*Y
∇

      3 ROUND2 4.5677887
4.568

      ROUND2 4.5677887
VALENCE ERROR
      ROUND2 4.5677887
      ^

      ⎕ET
5 1

      →

      )ERASE ROUND3
∇Z←Y ROUND3 X
 ⎕ES(2≠⎕NC 'Y')/5 4  ⍝SIGNAL DOMAIN ERROR
 Z←X
∇

      ROUND3 4.5677887
DOMAIN ERROR
      ROUND3 4.5677887
      ^

      ⎕ET
5 4

      →

      ]EXPECT 1

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #71, 2026-08-11): ⎕ES accepted
      ⍝ out-of-range major/minor codes and leaked an internal message.
      ⍝ get_error_code() packs B[0]/B[1] into a single 32-bit ErrorCode as
      ⍝ (major<<16)|minor with no range check, so e.g. ⎕ES 1E9 1E9 wrapped
      ⍝ to garbage (⎕ET came out ¯1126 51712) instead of DOMAIN ERROR; and
      ⍝ event_simulate() treated ANY B mapping to E_USER_DEFINED_ERROR's
      ⍝ own code (major/minor 0 1) as if B itself were the character
      ⍝ message text -- true only for the DEDICATED "⎕ES 'text'" case --
      ⍝ so a purely numeric ⎕ES 0 1 crashed into an internal cell-type
      ⍝ assertion whose text then leaked into )MORE.
      ⍝
      ⎕ES 0 1
User defined error
      ⎕ES 0 1
      ^
      )MORE
NO )MORE ERROR INFO
      ⎕ET
0 1
      )SIC

      ⍝ out of the representable 0..65535 range: now DOMAIN ERROR
      ⍝
      ⎕ES 1E9 1E9
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕ES 1000000000 1000000000
      ^
      )SIC

      ⎕ES ¯5 ¯4
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕ES ¯5 ¯4
      ^
      )SIC

      ⍝ control: in range but with no defined ⎕ET text is still accepted
      ⍝ with a blank message (LRM p.284), and the existing major=100
      ⍝ (⎕EA/⎕EB internal marker range) check is unaffected
      ⍝
      ⎕ES 99 99
      ⎕ES 99 99
      ^
      ⎕ET
99 99
      )SIC

      ⎕ES 100 1
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕ES 100 1
      ^
      )SIC

      ⍝ ==================================

